{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd","id":761792,"title":"How does Regeneration work in 2nd?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-09T15:59:43-08:00","id":761792,"title":"How does Regeneration work in 2nd?","content":"My group and I are new to 2nd Edition Forsaken and we were trying to puzzle out how exactly Regeneration is suppose to work mechanically during combat rounds, and here are some of the Questions that came up.<br /> <br /> 1) Do Werewolves Regenerate on their Turn, or at the end of the Round?<br /> <br /> 2) Spending Essence to upgrade Regeneration from Bashing to Lethal can be done Reflexively, does that mean the Werewolf can only do so during their Turn or can a Werewolf decide to spend that Essence at anytime during the Round?<br /> <br /> 3) What happens to a Werewolf when their Health Boxes are full of Lethal Damage or Bashing Damage? Do they Fall unconscious? Do they ignore it except for the Wound Penalties and keep on their feet fighting, fleeing, or what have you?<br /> <br /> 4) It says that so long as a Werewolf can Regenerate their Right Most Health Box they will not bleed out, we ask if you need to have Essence to spend to upgrade Regeneration to healing Lethal for this to be effective? If a Werewolf with no Essence to spend has his Right Most Health Box filled, are they as likely to bleed out as a normal person?<br /> <br /> 5) Can a Werewolf be knocked Unconscious, and if so would being Unconscious prevent a Werewolf from entering Garu form to activate their amazing Regenerative abilities in that form?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:20:36-08:00","id":761812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group and I are new to 2nd Edition Forsaken and we were trying to puzzle out how exactly Regeneration is suppose to work mechanically during combat rounds, and here are some of the Questions that came up.<br /> <br /> 1) Do Werewolves Regenerate on their Turn, or at the end of the Round?</div> </div> </div> </div>Start of the turn. Rounds aren't really a thing in 2e nwod, mechanically speaking. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Spending Essence to upgrade Regeneration from Bashing to Lethal can be done Reflexively, does that mean the Werewolf can only do so during their Turn or can a Werewolf decide to spend that Essence at anytime during the Round?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's at the exact moment their healing would occur normally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) What happens to a Werewolf when their Health Boxes are full of Lethal Damage or Bashing Damage? Do they Fall unconscious? Do they ignore it except for the Wound Penalties and keep on their feet fighting, fleeing, or what have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this one I'm not certain about, but I think that the roll to stay concious happens at the beginning of the turn the injured character would otherwise act, so in general a werewolf will heal the damage just before they need to roll. If their healing is somehow suppressed they will fall unconscious just like a a mortal though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) It says that so long as a Werewolf can Regenerate their Right Most Health Box they will not bleed out, we ask if you need to have Essence to spend to upgrade Regeneration to healing Lethal for this to be effective? If a Werewolf with no Essence to spend has his Right Most Health Box filled, are they as likely to bleed out as a normal person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <i>Mostly.</i> Without essence a werewolf will upgrade one lethal wound to aggravated per minute, while it will take them fifteen minutes to heal their rightmost lethal. This means that if they have more than fifteen health in hishu (Difficult, but not impossible) it will be possible for them to heal and cease bleeding out before they die. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Can a Werewolf be knocked Unconscious, and if so would being Unconscious prevent a Werewolf from entering Garu form to activate their amazing Regenerative abilities in that form?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*Shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:39:08-08:00","id":761826,"title":"","content":"They can be stunned I imagine they can be knocked out.<br /> <br /> That shouldn't affect their normal healing though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:06:41-08:00","id":761847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Do Werewolves Regenerate on their Turn, or at the end of the Round?</div> </div> </div> </div>Start of their turn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Spending Essence to upgrade Regeneration from Bashing to Lethal can be done Reflexively, does that mean the Werewolf can only do so during their Turn or can a Werewolf decide to spend that Essence at anytime during the Round?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say you got a 4L blast from a shotgun to your chest, on your turn you blow 2 essence, 1 for healing and one for shifting, this happens before you take your instant action. If your Primal Urge is 4, you heal 2L out of 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) What happens to a Werewolf when their Health Boxes are full of Lethal Damage or Bashing Damage? Do they Fall unconscious? Do they ignore it except for the Wound Penalties and keep on their feet fighting, fleeing, or what have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're full of bashing, they regenerate normally and do not fall unconscious. If they are full of lethal, they can spend essence and there isn't any unconsciousness roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) It says that so long as a Werewolf can Regenerate their Right Most Health Box they will not bleed out, we ask if you need to have Essence to spend to upgrade Regeneration to healing Lethal for this to be effective? If a Werewolf with no Essence to spend has his Right Most Health Box filled, are they as likely to bleed out as a normal person?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Elfive said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd#post761792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Can a Werewolf be knocked Unconscious, and if so would being Unconscious prevent a Werewolf from entering Garu form to activate their amazing Regenerative abilities in that form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they have no means to regenerate lethal damage, and they fail the unconsciousness roll, and don't use their action to go Gauru. So, yeah, quite hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:52:05-08:00","id":761954,"title":"","content":"That's assuming the damage dealt at that point doesn't force them into kuruth either. That can happen at what... 3 lethal? Furthest health boxes for sure. It's not like you'll get to just beat on one of the people without a fursplosion happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T20:01:04-08:00","id":761958,"title":"","content":"I don't think an unconscious werewolf can go gauru on their own, but I do believe there's some magic ways to force the matter, for better or worse. The Chain Rage rite has the subject immediately enter Wasu-Im if the focus is broken or taken, and the elodoth auspice ability Darkness Into Light could probably manage it, if a packmate is knocked unconscious for whatever reason and you need them to death rage right then.<br /> <br /> You could have them not rage until they wake up, but I think rule of cool would side with the raging spirit of the wolf bursting out of the unconscious human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:56:01-08:00","id":762423,"title":"","content":"Nah I'm saying per mechanics that once you enter the right 3 boxes of health you have death rage triggers. In order to get around that you gotta hit a werewolf with massive damage upside the head and hope you one shot em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:03:50-08:00","id":762435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=762423#post762423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah I'm saying per mechanics that once you enter the right 3 boxes of health you have death rage triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually listed as being a trigger in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:08:00-08:00","id":762436,"title":"","content":"Taking damage in the last boxes was a death rage trigger in first edition but not second. You could take it as your personal trigger, though.<br /> <br /> In any case I was talking about unconscious werewolves, not necessarily beaten unconscious ones. Such as you might get from Demon's Knockout Punch, the Choke Hold maneuver, a vampire commanding them to sleep, mage hijinx and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:01:14-08:00","id":762538,"title":"","content":"Oh I was thinking of mortals. And I was fairly certain it was listed in second editions pile of &quot;this effects everyone&quot; triggers. I'll have to look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:02:04-08:00","id":810036,"title":"","content":"Can reflexive actions such as spending essence to heal lethal actually happen <b>AFTER</b> you have been knocked unconscious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:40:47-08:00","id":810051,"title":"","content":"I think so, yeah. Actually knocking an Uratha unconscious due to trauma is virtually impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:46:06-08:00","id":810055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810051#post810051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so, yeah. Actually knocking an Uratha unconscious due to trauma is virtually impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page number? I believe you, but I have been searching for an hour to find anything about it.<br /> The rules also mention rolling to resist unconsciousness at full bashing, but not full lethal. Which is weird.<br /> I can't find the rules for being unconscious, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T23:33:45-08:00","id":810107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810036#post810036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can reflexive actions such as spending essence to heal lethal actually happen <b>AFTER</b> you have been knocked unconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>By rules as written, I'd say not. WtF 2nd p.169 says 'A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out. In other forms, werewolves take damage as humans do, though they have incredible regenerative powers.' The implication is that other forms can fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> Although p.160 says 'a reflexive action is the sort of thing you don't even need to think about doing', I believe that sentence is being colloquial, and you technically do have to be able to devote a modicum of conscious thought to doing an action reflexively. You certainly couldn't justify activating all your reflexive Facets one after the other if you were unconscious, unless they specified they activated that way. <br /> <br /> Note that the Uratha should be able to reflexively trigger her lethal regeneration powers any time before she falls unconscious - such as just before she makes the Stamina roll to see if she does pass out. My ruling would be that if she does that, she regenerates lethal while unconscious. If she chooses to trust the luck of the dice, and see what the Stamina roll brings, if she fails it's too late and she's on the ground only regenerating at the standard rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T00:38:19-08:00","id":810127,"title":"","content":"I believe in 1E you <i>could </i>in fact regenerate while unconscious, like vampires can. That's certainly how I run it, anyway. They regenerate passively while unconscious, and given the description of werewolf healing, I don't see why you couldn't spend Essence to regenerate faster while unconscious. It's not necessarily a conscious decision on the werewolf's part, even if the player is the one choosing to do so. It's the survival instinct kicked up to 11 in response to a grave threat. The intention is that werewolves are terribly hard to put down without silver, powerful magic, or a ton of firepower. Also, page 171 implies if anything that the werewolf <i>can </i>regenerate while unconscious: &quot;The only exception is if a human character has started bleeding out because her Health boxes are full of lethal damage. She can't recover from that without urgent medical attention and emergency surgery. As long as a werewolf can regenerate her rightmost Health box, she won't bleed out.&quot; That passage wouldn't make sense if you couldn't spend Essence to regenerate while unconscious from lethal damage.<br /> <br /> You might knock a werewolf out, but it will not last for long. They heal at least 1B every turn, so if you have their Health track full of bashing damage and they fail the Stamina roll, they'll still wake up the next turn regardless. If you knock them down with lethal, they might slump over, seemingly dead and bloodied ... then leap back up and attack before you realize that she's not dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T01:41:01-08:00","id":810139,"title":"","content":"I pretty much 100% disagree with you on this one Claire. Spending Essence is always a conscious choice. Even when the action is reflexive, it requires the tiniest amount of thought to do it. This can't happen when unconscious.<br /> <br /> p. 171 says nothing to negate this. Nothing stops a werewolf from regenerating. They always regenerate. While unconscious, they'll regenerate 1B per turn, and 1L every 15 minutes. As long as the werewolf can regenerate her rightmost box means that she'll be back up in very little time, but not instantly. That exact sentence makes perfect sense without needing to spend essence while unconscious.<br /> <br /> The way I'd suggest running it is that the werewolf won't bleed out at all. If she fails the Stamina roll, she falls unconscious from the lethal damage (with whatever wraps around into aggravated), and that's as far as it goes. As long as enemies don't keep attacking her, she doesn't keep adding damage until she dies. After 15 minutes she regenerates that right-most lethal box and wakes up. If she spent the essence immediately before falling unconscious, she regenerates that box next turn and wakes up.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd also suggest that if the intention was for Uratha to keep bouncing back instantly from unconsciousness, we wouldn't have written they behaved exactly like humans in forms other than Gauru. We'd probably have said something like:<br /> <br /> The Uratha's regenerative powers refuse to allow her to succumb to unconsciousness for long. A werewolf never makes a Stamina roll to check for unconsciousness from basking or lethal damage as long as she has Essence. For bashing, she slumps for a moment until her regeneration forces her back into the fight. For lethal, she drops for a moment as her body instinctively kicks into overdrive to regenerate lethal damage. Either way, the Uratha is awake and ready to act next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-16-2016, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:47:15-08:00","id":810153,"title":"","content":"Doesn't both healing and the unconsciousness roll happen at the start of their turn? I've always had the impression that by RAW they never get the chance to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:48:30-08:00","id":810154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810139#post810139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pretty much 100% disagree with you on this one Claire. Spending Essence is always a conscious choice. Even when the action is reflexive, it requires the tiniest amount of thought to do it. This can't happen when unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken 1st Edition, p. 168</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player may even spend Essence reflexively to regenerate points of lethal damage when her character is unconscious and bleeding to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the 1E core, but since the overall intent was to make werewolves tougher, this is the most likely interpretation of the 2E rules. Especially in conjunction with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken 2nd Edition, p. 160</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <i>reflexive </i>action is the sort of thing you don't even need to think about doing. Most rolls to resist supernatural powers are reflexive. You can take a reflexive action at any time, and it doesn't take your turn in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken 2nd Edition, p. 94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha heal their <b>regeneration</b> rate in points of lethal damage every 15 minutes. By spending a point of Essence as a <b>reflexive action</b>, she may <b>regenerate</b> lethal damage instead of bashing damage for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves spend Essence to heal reflexively. The same term is used for both types of healing, fast and &quot;slow.&quot; It's all regeneration. This is something they can do reflexively, which doesn't necessitate conscious thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810139#post810139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 171 says nothing to negate this. Nothing stops a werewolf from regenerating. They always regenerate. While unconscious, they'll regenerate 1B per turn, and 1L every 15 minutes. As long as the werewolf can regenerate her rightmost box means that she'll be back up in very little time, but not instantly. That exact sentence makes perfect sense without needing to spend essence while unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 171 all but negates your premise, because the only way a werewolf could otherwise live long enough to regenerate lethal damage while unconscious and bleeding out is if she had more than 15 Health. The idea was never that only the absolute most powerful werewolves could survive being incapacitated with lethal damage. Trust me on that one. I worked on the book, and even had input on the healing section. A sentence about werewolves being able to heal reflexively while bleeding out didn't make it in for whatever reason, but it's the intent, I assure you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810139#post810139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I'd suggest running it is that the werewolf won't bleed out at all. If she fails the Stamina roll, she falls unconscious from the lethal damage (with whatever wraps around into aggravated), and that's as far as it goes. As long as enemies don't keep attacking her, she doesn't keep adding damage until she dies. After 15 minutes she regenerates that right-most lethal box and wakes up. If she spent the essence immediately before falling unconscious, she regenerates that box next turn and wakes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fine enough rule, too. At least the werewolf isn't hosed if she gets incapacitated by lethal damage; the idea of buffing werewolves in 2nd edition runs counter to them getting taken out <i>more </i>easily than in 1st edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-16-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:47:53-08:00","id":810193,"title":"","content":"I'm with Claire. Reflexive was always meant to be something that can happen even when you don't know about it, like resisting supernatural powers that you are unaware of. The Stamina + Primal Urge always occur, unless you choose to allow the power to take effect. So, the conscious decision would be to STOP HEALING, not to ACCELERATE HEALING.<br /> <br /> As long as Essence is in their body, regeneration will use it to the benefit of the Uratha, specially when she is unconscious and can't force otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T06:43:17-08:00","id":810209,"title":"","content":"I'm personally not comfortable assuming anything from 1e books. Especially not with how regeneration works now. Now, I don't spend a lot of time in combat when I game. Its not my favorite part of the game. But I find the idea of a werewolf punching bag (knocked down, back up, knock down, back up) to be rather silly. So far, its hasn't come up - most of us shift to Gauru if we're in that much danger. In fact, the one time that a wolf got knocked out, our ST allowed reflexive shifting into Gauru, which solved the health issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:17:13-08:00","id":810232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810209#post810209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find the idea of a werewolf punching bag (knocked down, back up, knock down, back up) to be rather silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>He drinks a whisky drink, he drinks a vodka drink. He drinks a lager drink, he drinks a cider drink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:23:12-08:00","id":810236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810209#post810209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally not comfortable assuming anything from 1e books. Especially not with how regeneration works now. Now, I don't spend a lot of time in combat when I game. Its not my favorite part of the game. But I find the idea of a werewolf punching bag (knocked down, back up, knock down, back up) to be rather silly. So far, its hasn't come up - most of us shift to Gauru if we're in that much danger. In fact, the one time that a wolf got knocked out, our ST allowed reflexive shifting into Gauru, which solved the health issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, you just had the input of someone who explicitly worked on that part of the book saying the intent was to keep that particular bit like it was in 1e.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:39:52-08:00","id":810244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810236#post810236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, you just had the input of someone who explicitly worked on that part of the book saying the intent was to keep that particular bit like it was in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div> And yet, that's not what Clair said if you actually read what was written. And yet, the point of my post was to convey personal experience and feelings on the matter, not try to convince anyone of the exact rules.<br /> <br /> Even if you felt I wasn't listening to a developer,there are nicer ways to put it that don't feel antagonistic here. And its not the first time. Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-16-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T09:02:58-08:00","id":810253,"title":"","content":"Have to say, I do think &quot;punched back into Hishu&quot; should be something that only happens at the end of a fight. Makes the bigger forms too much of a potential liability otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T11:29:47-08:00","id":810302,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin I just want you to know that I greatly appreciate that comment. <br /> <br /> On topic I do like the idea of a werewolf getting back up when you thought he was donefor. Even though you no longer spend an essence to heal damage, but instead spend an essence to turn your healing from bashing into lethal I think it makes sense for an unconsicous werewolf to start reflexively healing whatever major damage he's sustained - and while whoever downed him is busy talking about what to do with the body he starts twitching a finger, and then starts growling and by the time they realize they're standing too close he tears off one of their arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T12:13:53-08:00","id":810319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810302#post810302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin I just want you to know that I greatly appreciate that comment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad someone caught on, I was worried I might have gone a bit too subtle with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810302#post810302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic I do like the idea of a werewolf getting back up when you thought he was donefor. Even though you no longer spend an essence to heal damage, but instead spend an essence to turn your healing from bashing into lethal I think it makes sense for an unconsicous werewolf to start reflexively healing whatever major damage he's sustained - and while whoever downed him is busy talking about what to do with the body he starts twitching a finger, and then starts growling and by the time they realize they're standing too close he tears off one of their arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is indeed very thematic for horror movie type werewolves, though I do wonder if the chumbawumba wolf might take what's an epic moment in small numbers and make it comedic through too much repetition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T12:56:17-08:00","id":810328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810154#post810154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the 1E core, but since the overall intent was to make werewolves tougher, this is the most likely interpretation of the 2E rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully, I disagree. I consider 1E irrelevant for anything that we have a 2E version of. The intent was to make werewolves tougher, yes. That's why we beefed Gauru. That's the point of its massive regeneration and immunity to unconsciousness. Werewolf was never meant to be that scene from Highlander, so Hishu get stabbed, groan and slump, then immediately stand up and giggle. Werewolves concerned about the real risk of succumbing to their wounds and failing their back burn Essence before waiting for the Stamina roll, or they go Gauru, with all the risks that entails. Gauru is meant to be the double-edged sword, the constant temptation. It's meant to be more like The Avengers - when you release the Hulk, you'll win, but will it be worth the cost?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810154#post810154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trust me on that one. I worked on the book, and even had input on the healing section. A sentence about werewolves being able to heal reflexively while bleeding out didn't make it in for whatever reason, but it's the intent, I assure you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. I was there. This specific scenario never came up, and I know that 2E places great importance on the purpose of each form. Every form has regeneration, Gauru is the *I will not yield* form. <br /> <br /> I'm not about making Uratha weaker in 2E, but I am about drama and player choice. Uratha have the risk of falling unconscious and being captured by their foes. That's drama - it makes the pack fight harder, think harder, and consider the risks going into battle. If the player wants to risk it all on the Sta roll, go ahead, but that's the drama of letting the dice decide. If she wants to guarantee another round, spend that Essence before making the roll. If she's already spent Essence this turn and can't spend more, that's the consequence of her choices as well. If her Harmony is right, she can choose to shift to Gauru in this instance. <br /> <br /> IMO, the sentence about reflexive actions requiring no thought (and therefore being possible when unconscious) is us writers being a little flippant with language and not considering at the time situations like we have here. <br /> <br /> As usual, I'd advise groups to use whichever interpretation best suits their game, but apply it consistently. Neither interpretation will break the setting, but each will open up tactical opportunities, while closing others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T13:37:04-08:00","id":810340,"title":"","content":"With all due respect (and I mean that sincerely), your argument has precious little backing it, and a lot of circumstantial evidence against it (I wish that line had made it in there).<br /> <br /> 1) Werewolves regenerate regardless of whether they're conscious. The sped up version of regeneration, where Essence burns to supercharge it, is still part of their natural regeneration. The fluff describing it, as well as the rules, explicitly tell us that it's not even something a werewolf fully controls. It's the survival need of the predator kicked up to 11.<br /> 2) Reflexive actions don't always need to be a conscious decision. Otherwise, should you automatically fail any resistance roll to a supernatural power you can neither see coming nor anticipate?<br /> 3) An explicit design goal in 2E was to make werewolves much tougher. This precludes taking away one of their biggest strengths from 1E Forsaken.<br /> 3a) I don't know how anyone would think a werewolf getting knocked down, and rising again every time is comedic. It'd be terrifying if you're in that combat. You put the beast down, you think you're safe, she's up again and attacking. Your weapons can't stop her. This was something mentioned in the 1E book, as well, about how attackers might feel they're safe, only for the werewolf to lash out again.<br /> 4) <i>Gauru </i>is only usable once a scene and never once described as the sole method by which werewolves can survive lethal damage. It <i>is</i> stated that <i>Gauru </i>form werewolves don't have to roll to remain conscious and won't bleed out, though the latter is a consequence of the fact that they'll regenerate all their lethal damage every turn.<br /> <br /> I will admit the book lacks a line clearly stating whether werewolves can spend Essence to regenerate while unconscious and bleeding out. There's a whole lot of stuff heavily implying (or outright saying, if you read the stuff I quoted as being a direct statement) that werewolves <i>can </i>do this, and not very much to imply that they can't. I did email Stew to get his thoughts on the matter, but he's a busy man so we might not hear back for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:08:56-08:00","id":810348,"title":"","content":"I'm entirely fine with Uratha being universally able to go &quot;you won't catch me alive&quot; mode.<br /> <br /> Pure wanna kidnap them? They better come up with fetishes for that explicit purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:12:39-08:00","id":810350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810340#post810340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect (and I mean that sincerely), your argument has precious little backing it, and a lot of circumstantial evidence against it (I wish that line had made it in there).<br /> <br /> 1) Werewolves regenerate regardless of whether they're conscious. The sped up version of regeneration, where Essence burns to supercharge it, is still part of their natural regeneration. The fluff describing it, as well as the rules, explicitly tell us that it's not even something a werewolf fully controls. It's the survival need of the predator kicked up to 11.<br /> 2) Reflexive actions don't always need to be a conscious decision. Otherwise, should you automatically fail any resistance roll to a supernatural power you can neither see coming nor anticipate?<br /> 3) An explicit design goal in 2E was to make werewolves much tougher. This precludes taking away one of their biggest strengths from 1E Forsaken.<br /> 3a) I don't know how anyone would think a werewolf getting knocked down, and rising again every time is comedic. It'd be terrifying if you're in that combat. You put the beast down, you think you're safe, she's up again and attacking. Your weapons can't stop her. This was something mentioned in the 1E book, as well, about how attackers might feel they're safe, only for the werewolf to lash out again.<br /> 4) <i>Gauru </i>is only usable once a scene and never once described as the sole method by which werewolves can survive lethal damage. It <i>is</i> stated that <i>Gauru </i>form werewolves don't have to roll to remain conscious and won't bleed out, though the latter is a consequence of the fact that they'll regenerate all their lethal damage every turn.<br /> <br /> I will admit the book lacks a line clearly stating whether werewolves can spend Essence to regenerate while unconscious and bleeding out. There's a whole lot of stuff heavily implying (or outright saying, if you read the stuff I quoted as being a direct statement) that werewolves <i>can </i>do this, and not very much to imply that they can't. I did email Stew to get his thoughts on the matter, but he's a busy man so we might not hear back for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have some worries about how Uratha are in 2e(going to wait until we have rules for other game lines including Mummy in 2e) I think you're right on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:22:51-08:00","id":810355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810348#post810348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm entirely fine with Uratha being universally able to go &quot;you won't catch me alive&quot; mode.<br /> <br /> Pure wanna kidnap them? They better come up with fetishes for that explicit purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or use poisons that can overcome even a werewolf's regeneration (there are some, at least until you get to really high power levels), powers that might render a werewolf helpless, etc. Or put a werewolf in a situation that she knows she can't get out of without dire consequences (like the killing of a pack member), so she comes along willingly. Trying to bludgeon a werewolf into unconsciousness pretty much doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810350#post810350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I have some worries about how Uratha are in 2e(going to wait until we have rules for other game lines including Mummy in 2e) I think you're right on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, although my wording may have been more hostile than was intended. Bunyip: totally friendly disagreement here. No disrespect meant at all, nor arguments made in anger. I just feel 100% confident that this was the intent, but if Stew comes back and says otherwise, I'll accept that I was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:29:43-08:00","id":810358,"title":"","content":"Edit: Also non hostile intent, but concerned that's not coming across in text format. <br /> <br /> til;dr - I disagree, look forward to hearing what Stew thinks, and don't want to drag this further into a he said/she said, so won't continue going back and forth on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I disagree with your characterisation of my argument (big surprise there), much as I think you're reaching at non-supportive or irrelevant text to support your argument. <br /> <br /> 1) Lethal regeneration is natural and an unconscious action. It's always happening at a rate of 1L/15 minutes. Overcharging it by specifically pumping Essence into the regeneration pathway is a conscious choice. <br /> <br /> 2) I agree that reflexive actions don't always need to be conscious decisions. I argue that this one does. <br /> <br /> 3) Yes, the design decision was to make the werewolf package tougher. That didn't mean leaving everything from 1E and bolting on more. It meant thinking about which parts made the package tougher, and made for a better game. We also removed armour from Gauru and high level Gifts. That didn't make the package weaker, and IMO, neither does this. <br /> <br /> 4) We're not talking about sole methods of surviving lethal damage. As stated before, every character has the choice to overdrive regeneration before checking for unconsciousness. If she has already spent all her essence for the turn, or chooses to risk the dice, that's drama. If she keels over unconscious, that's something her pack has to deal with. It's a trivial matter for them to bind her wounds and give her regeneration the 15 minutes it needs, but maybe that's difficult depending on if they're still in the middle of combat. Do they fight on, confident that they'll win before she bleeds out so they can help her, or do they grab her rag-doll form and run? Drama.<br /> Same with Gauru form. If you're in a scene where you've already taken Gauru and allowed it to lapse, then need it for more combat, that's either your very poor tactical planning, or very good tactical planning from your enemies. Once again, this increases the drama. If the whole pack has done this, you have real problems. Otherwise you have the nuclear option of letting one packmate head into Gauru then Kuruth, and everyone follow her into the carnage. <br /> <br /> If I'm wrong I'm wrong. I think my interpretation is more interesting, but I look forward to hearing what Stew says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-16-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:09:45-08:00","id":810988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810355#post810355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or use poisons that can overcome even a werewolf's regeneration (there are some, at least until you get to really high power levels), powers that might render a werewolf helpless, etc. Or put a werewolf in a situation that she knows she can't get out of without dire consequences (like the killing of a pack member), so she comes along willingly. Trying to bludgeon a werewolf into unconsciousness pretty much doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Pure werewolves making a looong harrying ordeal for their werewolf target, explicitly to harass, weaken, wound and continually drive their werewolf target to exhaustion until their werewolf target is out of Essence, weakened, and worn out.<br /> <br /> You know, be hunters and hunt their target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T00:53:37-08:00","id":811027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810988#post810988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Pure werewolves making a looong harrying ordeal for their werewolf target, explicitly to harass, weaken, wound and continually drive their werewolf target to exhaustion until their werewolf target is out of Essence, weakened, and worn out.<br /> <br /> You know, be hunters and hunt their target?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another good point. It'll be a long, bloody affair, grueling in a way nothing in the animal kingdom can match. For werewolf-on-werewolf violence, this is how it should be. You don't run down a werewolf without bringing some serious firepower and serious staying power, because if there's one thing werewolves do, it's endure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T01:30:55-08:00","id":811038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810988#post810988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the Pure werewolves making a looong harrying ordeal for their werewolf target, explicitly to harass, weaken, wound and continually drive their werewolf target to exhaustion until their werewolf target is out of Essence, weakened, and worn out.<br /> <br /> You know, be hunters and hunt their target?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one example of what I described when I wrote 'If you're in a scene where you've already taken Gauru and allowed it to lapse, then need it for more combat, that's either your very poor tactical planning, or very good tactical planning from your enemies.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T01:44:06-08:00","id":811039,"title":"","content":"It just occurred to me that groups who choose to follow the 'can't spend while unconscious' path could introduce a new merit covering this. Uratha with this merit will overcharge their regeneration whenever they fall unconscious, as long as they have Essence. <br /> <br /> Drawback... I'd say the unconscious overcharge isn't as fine tuned as conscious control - the character must also spend a point of Essence at the beginning of the next turn to keep her regeneration high. This counts towards how much Essence she can spend in that turn, and may prevent her from taking other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:05:59-08:00","id":811150,"title":"","content":"Since Kuruth isn't triggered by near death anymore, I assume that a Werewolf that has spent Gauru is in a pretty dire situation. Can he force Kuruth in anyway? I imagine that carrying a small silver blade to hurt yourself would be a common tradition among Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:52:14-08:00","id":811171,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Death Rage is always an option&quot; makes for werewolfier werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:21:39-08:00","id":811288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811150#post811150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Kuruth isn't triggered by near death anymore, I assume that a Werewolf that has spent Gauru is in a pretty dire situation. Can he force Kuruth in anyway? I imagine that carrying a small silver blade to hurt yourself would be a common tradition among Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if you were subjected to Chain Rage, divesting yourself of it's amulet focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:37:07-08:00","id":811299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811171#post811171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;Death Rage is always an option&quot; makes for werewolfier werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I'm going to allow it for my players. I'm a fan of Werewolves that are always repressing their rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811171#post811171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if you were subjected to Chain Rage, divesting yourself of it's amulet focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least once after every use, yes. I assume this rite is a powerful tool to convince young Uratha to join your tribe/pack, as it helps to control the Rage, and also gives you a mean to access it even when totally exhausted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:42:55-08:00","id":811332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811150#post811150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Kuruth isn't triggered by near death anymore, I assume that a Werewolf that has spent Gauru is in a pretty dire situation. Can he force Kuruth in anyway? I imagine that carrying a small silver blade to hurt yourself would be a common tradition among Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several ways. Various triggers, depending on his Harmony. The general triggers are always available - having a small silver knife available might be blasphemous, but stabbing yourself with it will get the job done. Your pack Elodoth can push you over the edge. You could have some stored up via Chain Rage. <br /> <br /> Technically though, I don't believe you can just say 'I feel like Kuruth now' in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:24:53-08:00","id":811403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811039#post811039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just occurred to me that groups who choose to follow the 'can't spend while unconscious' path could introduce a new merit covering this. Uratha with this merit will overcharge their regeneration whenever they fall unconscious, as long as they have Essence.<br /> <br /> Drawback... I'd say the unconscious overcharge isn't as fine tuned as conscious control - the character must also spend a point of Essence at the beginning of the next turn to keep her regeneration high. This counts towards how much Essence she can spend in that turn, and may prevent her from taking other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that interesting, and it wouldn't be that difficult of a thing, either.<br /> <br /> But imagine, some Pure hunting and harrying their Forsaken prey...wearing her down, thinking they've won...and then she gets up and tears into them as they're surprised and not defending themselves. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:48:52-08:00","id":811414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811332#post811332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several ways. Various triggers, depending on his Harmony. The general triggers are always available - having a small silver knife available might be blasphemous, but stabbing yourself with it will get the job done. Your pack Elodoth can push you over the edge. You could have some stored up via Chain Rage.<br /> <br /> Technically though, I don't believe you can just say 'I feel like Kuruth now' in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the dramatic opportunities of a Werewolf who can't always let himself enter Kuruth, but don't you agree that it feels strange that the risk of death won't set her up? Even with their regenerative abilities, it is quite possible to fill the health track of a Werewolf with lethal damage. I would say that at least at the very moment the last box is filled with lethal, she enters Wasu-Im. If she truly wishes to die without a fight, she should pass a Resolve+Composure roll and slide into death peacefully.<br /> <br /> Another take at it would be testing for Kuruth when the first lethal is upgraded to aggravated, but it gets a little bit more complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:26:12-08:00","id":811436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811414#post811414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the dramatic opportunities of a Werewolf who can't always let himself enter Kuruth, but don't you agree that it feels strange that the risk of death won't set her up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kuruth seems to be more about being the ultimate predator, not simply survival. You may be only able to enter gauru once a scene, but scenes can be short, especially with werewolves in gauru form around.<br /> <br /> As for your silver knife idea, I'd probably avoid something as obvious as that. Aggravated damage hurts, and you would only be weakening your gauru form and potentially giving any enemies around a weapon to kill you with. As an alternative, check out the Chain Rage rite. Your werewolf can ameliorate the deterioration of death rage, but with a simple act pushes you into it. For the cost of one experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T20:23:27-08:00","id":811504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811332#post811332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically though, I don't believe you can just say 'I feel like Kuruth now' in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd allow it. I like the feeling of keeping the rage from bursting out being a active effort. Any benefit that willing Kuruth could bring is heavily overshadowed by it's obvious risks. Specially if it could become something like an addiction. You know how hammers see every problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T23:12:11-08:00","id":811575,"title":"","content":"Sounds like another merit option, one with possible multiple levels. I'd base it around vampires' ability to ride the wave, only better tailored to werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T02:30:26-08:00","id":811626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811504#post811504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd allow it. I like the feeling of keeping the rage from bursting out being a active effort. Any benefit that willing Kuruth could bring is heavily overshadowed by it's obvious risks. Specially if it could become something like an addiction. You know how hammers see every problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with this scenario (and the bouncing ball lethal healing) is that it's essentially creep from Apocalypse to Forsaken. Apocalypse is 'When Will You Rage', Forsaken is 'The Wolf Must Hunt'. Your remark about hammers clearly defines this problem. Garou are hammers, Uratha are scalpels.<br /> <br /> Garou Rage. They're at war against the biggest cosmic evil of them all. They fight tooth and nail to the last because this is war, and war is hell. Every tool is a hammer, and every problem is treated like a nail and smashed. They take Crinos with impunity, they smash and hit and tear and destroy everything around them. They enter frenzies when injured and bounce back when nearly dead and unleash hell without thought - or fear, really. Garou are Gaia's warriors - they fight to win.<br /> <br /> Uratha hunt. This is important. The hunt is smart. The hunt is planned. The hunt is tactical. The hunt is working your advantage to gain the kill. The hunt is knowing your tools and employing each of them as needed. The hunt has sections, and everyone has a role. Uratha have specialised forms for different aspects of the hunt. Uratha have GIfts for different aspects of the hunt. Forsaken have Hunters Aspects, that enforce the prey's role in the hunt. Uratha are Gaia's apex predators - they hunt to win.<br /> <br /> When an Uratha is on the hunt, she's always thinking. She's in control. She commands this hunt. Kuruth is a factor, but so is everything else. If her enemies are smart, they'll try and remove her control, because that's one way to defeat her hunt. When she tracks the prey, she uses the best form. When she hides from the prey, she uses the best form. When she moves in for the kill, she takes the killing form - Gauru.<br /> <br /> If she takes Gauru and the prey outsmarts her, and outlasts her time in Gauru, she reassesses. How did the prey outlast? Was the prey too smart? Perhaps she needs to withdraw and rethink her hunting strategy. Did she underestimate the prey? Did she have this hunt wrong? Was she thinking too small, and she was the prey in a larger hunt all along? Was the prey too tough? She has another tool at her disposal, and can enter Kuruth as the final seconds of Gauru slip away, but this is a difficult choice. She'll likely win, but at what cost?<br /> <br /> The hunt is back-and-forth, cat-and-mouse. It can be one-sided. Uratha are awesome hunters. They can destroy lesser prey with ease. But we're not talking lesser prey. Why use Gauru on a simple kill unless you're proving a point? Uratha hunt the most dangerous prey. They hunt prey that requires skill, patience, and a holistic approach to their toolkit. They hunt prey who will try to turn tables on them, and they may become the hunted. <br /> <br /> They hunt prey where a legitimate tactic might be to 'kill' themselves (or have their pack do it), because they need 15 minutes of seeming death to get past whatever impenetrable barrier the prey has put in their way. They hunt prey that knows of their limitations, and works within those. If Uratha instantly bounce back every time they're put down without fail, their prey knows this and those Uratha won't be getting back up. If Uratha can enter Kuruth at any time without restriction, the prey knows this and will fight accordingly. These contests become win or die. These contests become war. Those Uratha are more like Garou than Uratha.<br /> <br /> Hunters work within their limitations. They understand their choices and use them as best they can. When Uratha have limited access to enter Kuruth, they know how to do it, they know how to weigh up the risks versus benefits, and they know when to make the choice.<br /> <br /> These are the Uratha I want to write. They're hunters, and they're more than scalpels, they're surgeons. They know what their tools are for and when to use them. They have hammers, but they know not every problem is a nail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T03:39:19-08:00","id":811652,"title":"","content":"by that reasoning gauru shouldn't be a thing at all.<br /> <br /> Urshul makes for a better form at killing than Gauru. Gauru is more of a survival mechanism.<br /> <br /> Edit: *coff*Elemental Gift*coff*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-19-2016, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:12:23-08:00","id":811661,"title":"","content":"That's just flat out not true. Gauru forces down and dirty combat. It can kill a whole bunch of people with one roll. That's objectively better at killing than Urshul can manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:31:46-08:00","id":811673,"title":"","content":"&quot;Forcing&quot; is not the best term there. It forces down and dirty on targets that are predisposed to being &quot;down and dirtied&quot; by any other form anyhow, by the reading of the mechanic itself.<br /> <br /> The draft of the mechanic for down and dirty combat over the God Machine Chronicle read that a character merely needed 5 dice worth in a combat dice pool to having &quot;internalized the mechanics of combat&quot; (Which Gauru provides quite handily assuming the character has at least Strength of 2). So any Uratha can pull that off with a meager dot of brawl under those circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:49:16-08:00","id":811682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811652#post811652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by that reasoning gauru shouldn't be a thing at all.<br /> <br /> Urshul makes for a better form at killing than Gauru. Gauru is more of a survival mechanism.<br /> <br /> Edit: *coff*Elemental Gift*coff*</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry Ephsy, but I believe you're just wrong here. Gauru has better regeneration, better damage, better Strength, better initiative, forces opponents to suffer reduced defence if they don't suffer Down &amp; Dirty outright. <br /> <br /> Gauru is a tool that functions very well for killing. A common part of Uratha hunting is being up close and personal with the prey to make the killing blow. Desperate, dangerous prey often struggle their hardest at this point. Uratha need all the survivability they can get to make the kill and walk away cleanly. Urshul weakens dangerous prey, Gauru kills it. <br /> <br /> Your comment about Gauru not being a thing implies you've either missed my point, or your ignoring it. Either way, more power to you running your game however you choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:55:48-08:00","id":811686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811673#post811673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Forcing&amp;quot; is not the best term there. It forces down and dirty on targets that are predisposed to being &amp;quot;down and dirtied&amp;quot; by any other form anyhow, by the reading of the mechanic itself.<br /> <br /> The draft of the mechanic for down and dirty combat over the God Machine Chronicle read that a character merely needed 5 dice worth in a combat dice pool to having &amp;quot;internalized the mechanics of combat&amp;quot; (Which Gauru provides quite handily assuming the character has at least Strength of 2). So any Uratha can pull that off with a meager dot of brawl under those circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Down &amp; Dirty Combat (p.165) - The Storyteller might decide... The Storyteller can opt to use...<br /> <br /> Gauru (p.97) - Gauru force all lesser enemies ... to use Down and Dirty combat (see p. 165).<br /> <br /> 'Forcing' is specifically the correct term here. Gauru explicitly removes the 'ST might decide' factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:29:59-08:00","id":811703,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't a storyteller allow any form to use down and dirty on clearly lesser foes? That's my point.<br /> <br /> Moot discussion anyway, because system-wise, there's nothing stopping me from A) Going gauru at any time I want before init, thus initiating Kuruth; or B) Going Gauru past it's time-frame, thus achieving Kuruth.<br /> <br /> Edit: Bear in mind, Bunyip, my scenario concerns itself with a particular character. Not with the setting at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-19-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:44:40-08:00","id":811744,"title":"","content":"Bundle of thoughts.<br /> <br /> I do think Werewolves should be able to regenerate lethal every round while unconscious, but I also think that Bunyip is right that if werewolves can wake up every round from being unconscious it not only feels like Whack-A-Mole but far more challenges will turn into absolutely lethal situations where a werewolf dies almost every time.<br /> <br /> The easy solution is a house rule. Yes, you can spend essence to regenerate while unconscious. No, you do not regain consciousness until you succeed at a Stamina + Resolve roll to snap yourself awake (wound penalties apply).<br /> <br /> I think Bunyip is wrong about Gauru being the killing form, though. That was obviously the design intent, but it almost never works out that way at the gaming table. You almost always want to save Gauru for as long as possible, to use the healing to save your life. In a fight between a bunch of werewolves this becomes super clear, because Urshal and Urhan have an easy time kiting the Gauru and making him waste turns uselessly chasing or attacking nothing in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:27:00-08:00","id":811822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811703#post811703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moot discussion anyway, because system-wise, there's nothing stopping me from A) Going gauru at any time I want before init, thus initiating Kuruth; or B) Going Gauru past it's time-frame, thus achieving Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not consider that possibility. By the rules as writen, nothing really stops you from turning into Gauru EVEN when your time-limit is is over. You will have to roll to avoid Kuruth as always, but nothing prohibits this. Effectively, Uratha might Death Rage whenever they like. Good point, Ephsy.<br /> <br /> Bunyip, my problem is with Werewolves that won't lose control to Risk-Of-Death scenarios, but at the same scene might hear a wolf howl to their auspice moon and enter <i>Wasu-Im</i> instantly. It just feels wrong. If Death Rage is really what is described by the book, it is always lurking at the mind of the Werewolf, always pushing him a little bit to the edge.<br /> <br /> And I really don't feel this approach goes against what you described: Uratha as Scalpels. The book goes to great lenghts to remind you that one pack member in <i>Kuruth</i> brings the others into it, and that the pack is more than Werewolves, it is about humans and Wolf-blooded kin that can't join you in the frenzy. Kuruth will almost always feel wrong to any Werewolf that wants to be sure he won't screw everything his pack is aiming for. Looking at Death Rage at life threatening situations like this, it feels even more risky: You can't approach the hunt in a caraless way and put yourself in risk, because if you fail, even if you don't die, your packmates will pay the full price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:33:27-08:00","id":811830,"title":"","content":"Just a thought: Would it change all that much to say that the Gauru time limit doesn't need to be spent in one go? Like, if you have five turns you could use three of them, switch back, and then later use the other two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:36:44-08:00","id":811831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811830#post811830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought: Would it change all that much to say that the Gauru time limit doesn't need to be spent in one go? Like, if you have five turns you could use three of them, switch back, and then later use the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, it would very much turn Gauru into the Healing Form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:19:34-08:00","id":811915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811831#post811831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it would very much turn Gauru into the Healing Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If Gauru should feel like a bomb or last resort, then being able to drop it in small doses goes right against the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:09:24-08:00","id":812000,"title":"","content":"Fair 'nuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:23:24-08:00","id":812058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811831#post811831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it would very much turn Gauru into the Healing Form.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm werewolfing wrong then. Dammit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:37:36-08:00","id":812068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811831#post811831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it would very much turn Gauru into the Healing Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is THAT what's been missing this entire time. I've seen the light!<br /> <br /> Coincidentally, all my games in Forsaken are going be about flower picking from now on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:58:57-08:00","id":812147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=811822#post811822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not consider that possibility. By the rules as writen, nothing really stops you from turning into Gauru EVEN when your time-limit is is over. You will have to roll to avoid Kuruth as always, but nothing prohibits this. Effectively, Uratha might Death Rage whenever they like. Good point, Ephsy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if I'm just misreading what you're saying, but the rules don't support what you're saying. Yes, you can turn into Gauru at any time in a scene. Yes, you can linger in Gauru too long and fall into Kuruth. What you can't do is go into Gauru, leave Gauru, then later decide to use the form again just to access Death Rage.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of triggers that might force you into Kuruth (and therefore Gauru), but that's not one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:20:56-08:00","id":812171,"title":"","content":"P97. 'She can take Gauru once per scene, and then only for a number of turns equal to her (Hishu) Stamina + Primal Urge.'<br /> <br /> If you've left gauru, it's off the table for the scene outside of triggers and other situations that can cause it, such as other werewolves entering death rage.<br /> <br /> Think predator. Not person with powers, some of which are regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:24:54-08:00","id":812176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=812147#post812147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if I'm just misreading what you're saying, but the rules don't support what you're saying. Yes, you can turn into Gauru at any time in a scene. Yes, you can linger in Gauru too long and fall into Kuruth. What you can't do is go into Gauru, leave Gauru, then later decide to use the form again just to access Death Rage.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of triggers that might force you into Kuruth (and therefore Gauru), but that's not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken, page 97</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=812147#post812147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolf can only hold on to the primal beast for so long. She can take Gauru once per scene, and then only for a number of turns equal to her (Hishu) Stamina + Primal Urge. After that point, she must choose: Shift down into Dalu or Urshul, or fall into Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. As written, one cannot take the Gauru even if he wants to risk Death Rage, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:27:14-08:00","id":812178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=812147#post812147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if I'm just misreading what you're saying, but the rules don't support what you're saying. Yes, you can turn into Gauru at any time in a scene. Yes, you can linger in Gauru too long and fall into Kuruth. What you can't do is go into Gauru, leave Gauru, then later decide to use the form again just to access Death Rage.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of triggers that might force you into Kuruth (and therefore Gauru), but that's not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the point made here is: if your objective is to fall to kuruth (unwise as it may be) you just have to go Gauru and/or linger in the form until it is achieved. No other trigger is necessary. That only applying when you hadn't, previously, used the form to it's full potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:16:19-08:00","id":812232,"title":"","content":"We're in agreement Ephsy. It was just BinAly's comments that I was unsure of. (Which he has now clarified.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:50:28-07:00","id":850318,"title":"","content":"The new regenerative powers make it difficult to actually kill a werewolf. I know it can be done but it just seems very tough now, especially since they can always revert to the Kuruth option and be invincible for a while. Here are some thoughts on how to actually bring a pile of hurt onto an uratha pack.<br /> <br /> 1/ The bite of a host might be a death sentence if they have the grave poisoned condition. I thought that, if the condition exists as long as the victim cannot get medical treatment, so the werewolf would first run out of essence, then go into the garou form. Once that finished, the werewolf would pretty much be dead.<br /> <br /> 2/ Outnumber the werewolves. Being outnumbered about 3 or 4 or 5 to 1 means that enough damage is being done to wrap the damage to aggravated. A swarm of hosts, or claimed, or spirits can do that.<br /> <br /> 3/ Silver bullets work nicely. Sure Pentex first teams no longer are part of the game but it means that adversaries, like hunters or claimed or vampires, can create their own bullets or other silver weapons.<br /> <br /> 4/ Other werewolves can bite for aggravated damage. <br /> <br /> One other thing that has not been mentioned as a drawback to Kuruth is that the werewolf collapses in their human form at the end. That needs elaboration since it suggests that the werewolf is in a very weakened state and can probably killed or captured easily then. Since they had just let loose a ton of rage it would seem that they would have exhausted their power and would be incapable of much then, probably being unconscious for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:00:02-07:00","id":850321,"title":"","content":"In my own game on RPOL, the pack just faced down a Beshilu Rokhan (basically, the big mutated versions) and a swarm it had summoned. Our Rahu was <i>seriously </i>hurt by the end of the fight, between being poisoned and torn into by gnashing rat teeth and so on. She ended up at about 9 lethal out of 12 health levels, and that was after burning lots of Essence to heal both grave poison and try to keep on top of the damage. She's still pretty bloodied and hurt, but also could have gone into Gauru at any point in that fight and made short work of the Beshilu. Any of the werewolves could have, but their natural toughness saw them through without needing to pull the trigger. Inside a few hours she'll be good as new without needing to spend Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T05:59:05-07:00","id":850516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=850321#post850321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own game on RPOL, the pack just faced down a Beshilu Rokhan (basically, the big mutated versions) and a swarm it had summoned. Our Rahu was <i>seriously </i>hurt by the end of the fight, between being poisoned and torn into by gnashing rat teeth and so on. She ended up at about 9 lethal out of 12 health levels, and that was after burning lots of Essence to heal both grave poison and try to keep on top of the damage. She's still pretty bloodied and hurt, but also could have gone into Gauru at any point in that fight and made short work of the Beshilu. Any of the werewolves could have, but their natural toughness saw them through without needing to pull the trigger. Inside a few hours she'll be good as new without needing to spend Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent example, but it also raises a lot of questions. Even if your characters were in trouble during the encounter, they could have simply pushed the &quot;garou&quot; button and, not only healed their damage, but also made short work of the Beshilu. That would have made a less than challenging encounter. <br /> <br /> The question I have, which I have been wondering about since 2nd edition came about, is how to make an encounter that will make the characters sweat. What kind of enemies do you need to throw at the pack to make them think that they might die, even if they push the garou/kuruth option. I imagine you need to take adversaries such as hosts/spirits/claimed and outnumber the pack about 2 to 1, or have about enemy werewolves in a ratio of 1 to 1 to make an encounter a challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:26:57-07:00","id":850534,"title":"","content":"Cannibalistic Anshega outnumbering them 2 to 1; Recurring spirits stealing your loved ones' bodies and urging you into kuruth to have you butcher them, off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T23:44:49-07:00","id":850992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=850516#post850516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an excellent example, but it also raises a lot of questions. Even if your characters were in trouble during the encounter, they could have simply pushed the &quot;garou&quot; button and, not only healed their damage, but also made short work of the Beshilu. That would have made a less than challenging encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's true. I knew that going in, though. The surprise was that the Rokhan was as brutal as it was, and nearly put our Rahu's back against the wall. She doggedly stuck with Dalu form unarmed combat, though, with which she is quite good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=850516#post850516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I have, which I have been wondering about since 2nd edition came about, is how to make an encounter that will make the characters sweat. What kind of enemies do you need to throw at the pack to make them think that they might die, even if they push the garou/kuruth option. I imagine you need to take adversaries such as hosts/spirits/claimed and outnumber the pack about 2 to 1, or have about enemy werewolves in a ratio of 1 to 1 to make an encounter a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have options for threatening encounters. 2-3 of those Beshilu plus more swarms or a filth-spirit ally might have helped, or a Claimed of the alleyways. I knew going in that the werewolves were going to dominate when it came time, though. It's part of the experience. Technically, an entire pack can take Gauru at once, making them very, <i>very </i>difficult to physically. This is working as intended. Werewolves are dangerous beyond belief, and generally once they run the prey to ground they kick its ass. Usually, the hunt itself is the real challenge. Some few things can still stand up to a pack regardless, but in many cases, this requires an out of context problem. Gauru can't help if you can't actually bite or claw your foe, or he doesn't attack you physically (perhaps using traps or illusions, mental assaults, etc.). A political campaign might be run by a Pure Wolf-Blooded with a grudge, and a position (with clout) that isn't easily torn apart by claws. Especially when his actions begin to cause widespread effects across the city's Shadow. Put the werewolves in a situation like a shootout at a campaign rally with the Senator's armed bodyguards, where they're in danger, but could rather easily defeat the threat by shifting into Gauru\u2014and doing so would cause as many problems as it would solve.<br /> <br /> Physically challenging an entire pack of werewolves can be difficult without completely destroying them. And even against things that can totally outclass them, like high-Rank spirits, werewolves have ways of evening up the score. But if a pack is desperate enough to use everything they have, well, sometimes, just sit back, let the dice roll and the blood flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T02:04:36-07:00","id":851028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=850516#post850516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an excellent example, but it also raises a lot of questions. Even if your characters were in trouble during the encounter, they could have simply pushed the &quot;garou&quot; button and, not only healed their damage, but also made short work of the Beshilu. That would have made a less than challenging encounter.<br /> <br /> The question I have, which I have been wondering about since 2nd edition came about, is how to make an encounter that will make the characters sweat. What kind of enemies do you need to throw at the pack to make them think that they might die, even if they push the garou/kuruth option. I imagine you need to take adversaries such as hosts/spirits/claimed and outnumber the pack about 2 to 1, or have about enemy werewolves in a ratio of 1 to 1 to make an encounter a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use opponents who like to dish out a lot of aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T03:35:58-07:00","id":851051,"title":"","content":"Also, there's no such thing as garou in Werewolf: The Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}